{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC \"the wheel and sdist contain no `evals/` entry\" **failed on first measurement**, caught by actually building the distributions rather than reasoning from the `include` allowlist.\n\n```\nwheel evals/ entries: 0\nsdist evals/ entries: 5\n```\n\nThe five are `evals/README.md`, `evals/code-grounding-spike/README.md`, `evals/plan-review-gate/README.md`, `evals/plan-review-gate/runs/README.md`, `evals/workflow-remediation-pocs/README.md`.\n\n**Root cause.** `[tool.hatch.build.targets.sdist] include = [\"src/rebar\", \"tests\", \"README.md\"]` — `\"README.md\"` is a **depth-agnostic glob** in hatchling, not a root-anchored path. Every `README.md` anywhere in the tree matches it, so the allowlist never excluded the corpus.\n\n**Pre-existing, not introduced here.** Built the sdist at the pre-move commit `aa37a738570` to check rather than assume; it already contained `docs/experiments/README.md`, `docs/experiments/code-grounding-spike/README.md`, `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/README.md`, `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/runs/README.md`, alongside `docs/README.md`, `docs/adr/README.md`, `docs/archive/README.md` and `.github/llm-providers/README.md`. The corpus move only renamed those paths, which is what made this ticket's own AC fail. The AC rested on a false premise — that the `include` allowlist kept the tree out of the sdist — and the plan review did not catch it because the premise was stated, not measured.\n\n**Fix** (follow-up change, since 3121 already merged and this ticket is still `in_progress`): add `/evals`, `evals`, `evals/**` to the sdist `exclude` list, mirroring the existing `infra` belt-and-suspenders entries, with a comment recording why the allowlist is insufficient. Re-measured: wheel `0`, sdist `0`, root `README.md` still shipped, all 941 `src/rebar/` entries still shipped.\n\nAdded `test_the_research_corpus_is_excluded_from_both_distributions` to `tests/unit/test_packaging_dependencies.py`, asserting the three exclude patterns are present and documenting the depth-agnostic-glob reason — without that note the next reader sees `include` and reasonably concludes the exclusion is redundant, then deletes it.\n\n**Adjacent finding, NOT fixed here.** The same glob still ships `docs/README.md`, `docs/adr/README.md`, `docs/archive/README.md` and `.github/llm-providers/README.md` in the sdist, none of which are named by the `include` allowlist's evident intent (`src/rebar`, `tests`, and the project README). That is a pre-existing packaging-hygiene question about files unrelated to this epic, so it is out of scope here rather than silently widened into this change."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793114199396232031,"uuid":"18c19ab7-23bc-4051-9408-99c2fa06e1ea"}